  "final_answer": "I have found an Italian-style meatball recipe on Allrecipes with more than 100 reviews. Here are the details:\n\n## Recipe Found: Chef John's Italian Meatballs\n\n**Source:** [https://www.allrecipes.com/recipe/220854/chef-johns-italian-meatballs/](https://www.allrecipes.com/recipe/220854/chef-johns-italian-meatballs/)\n\n### Key Details:\n\n**Reviews:** 1,964 Reviews (with 2,532 total ratings and 4.8 star average) — well over the 100-review threshold. ✓\n\n**Type of Meat Used:** A standard **half-beef/half-pork mixture** (i.e., a 50/50 blend of ground beef and ground pork). The recipe description specifically states: *\"Here I use a standard half-beef/half-pork mixture.\"*\n\n### Overall Cooking Time:\n\n| Component | Time |\n|-----------|------|\n| Prep Time | 20 mins |\n| Cook Time | 35 mins |\n| Additional Time | 1 hr 20 mins |\n| **Total Time** | **2 hrs 15 mins** |\n\n**The total overall cooking time is 2 hours and 15 minutes.** This includes 35 minutes of active cook time (baking the meatballs) plus the 1 hour 20 minutes of additional time, where the baked meatballs are simmered in your favorite prepared tomato sauce for 1–2 hours to finish.\n\n### Why this recipe qualifies:\n- ✅ It's an Italian-style meatball recipe (categorized under \"Italian Meatball Recipes\")\n- ✅ It has far more than 100 reviews (1,964 reviews)\n- ✅ Clear, source-backed information about both the meat type and cooking time",
